{# The mark at the top of every submission receipt.

   It used to be ◬ — the same glyph the Vote card uses for climbs — which read
   as a warning triangle above a line saying "Nothing appears on the map yet",
   so a successful contribution looked like an error report (owner-reported
   2026-08-07). A thumbs-up says the thing the page is actually for: it worked,
   and someone is grateful.

   Line art in currentColor rather than a filled icon or an emoji: it inherits
   the page's ink, renders identically on every platform, and needs no font.
   One partial, used by all four receipts, so the mark and the thanks cannot
   drift apart between them. #}
<div class="receipt-mark">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="46" height="46" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
       stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
       role="img" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <path d="M3.6 11.6h2.9v9.8H3.6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1v-7.8a1 1 0 0 1 1-1Z"/>
    <path d="M6.5 11.6 10.9 2.9a2.2 2.2 0 0 1 4.2 1V9h4.5a2 2 0 0 1 1.95 2.46l-1.7 7.4a2.4 2.4 0 0 1-2.34 1.86H8.5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2Z"/>
  </svg>
  {# A div, not a p: `.receipt p` is what the receipt tests select for the
     body copy, and a paragraph here silently became the first match. It is
     a label anyway. #}
  <div class="receipt-thanks">{{ 'receipt.thanks'|trans }}</div>
</div>
